uuid "2d9ef966-b8f1-5433-8fc3-084844d45df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124976" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{5}$ and $\\pi <\\theta <\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ then what is the value of $tan⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch our angle $\\theta $ in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/8761c66ecaef04f605c3c05b2274673b7b8de78763c224d795fbb000a5acc4b0.png)\n\nWe're given that $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{5}.$ We can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{5}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is negative in the third quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{4}{5}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{5})}{(-\\frac{4}{5})}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124976/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98d6004a-547a-5b0b-9748-9571cc3ee632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124976"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-23307/selection/d7bb718b0ec75ff2850926adad9e2b022a536d3b55243635ca4996ab7e504dd3" :answer/id #uuid "ca1bb7a0-028e-5816-aa81-8c8c1b748b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "tan⁡\\theta =-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23307/selection/722022665ecfd2092d79711b12f5af5af9ced5b5c6d14526dc6a8fc8002a154f" :answer/id #uuid "33b4bcea-a773-572c-a039-6601