oper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/7873579bb5dd1976330ec24f13b30dd384f916cf23bbf48aac4b2a522ee9548a.png)\n\nWe're given that $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{2}.$ We can use the Pythagorean identity to find $sin⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $sin⁡\\theta $ is negative in the third quadrant. So, $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-23307/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98d6004a-547a-5b0b-9748-9571cc3ee632"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-23307"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85643/selection/02bd85d8ef0eab243b5263b64b9ff5a329de46d7086d62c76e90e0b6d5401f96" :answer/id #uuid "f5f83147-6fbc-5ed2-bde7-45d9b85616dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{6}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85643/selection/a3d13a5807221d895018d7b06558d926d62bfb001b459077c27b527e0d873fba" :answer/id #uuid "01e39e5c-1b12-57ef-a0b8-efbe7b69e901" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85643/selection/2ddda6672cd9117c496b40039bb24e9551b86514a0ced6b2d869664914795cff" :answer/id #uuid "28690b26-9b29-56dd-8683-e436142a1c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85643/selection/fbc9f6433e70c687e4cd524a01759124f3a0b394750ef110b890774618ad4f45" :answer/id #uuid "1e33194e-4c90-5549-be8f-b39afd15162d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85643/selection/250d160b15e9359628e412b91e5c1fd679c52d57a82017145d130d6c7fa4646e" :answer/id #uuid "185b02c7-c0dc-5868-b578-ece8b1347e6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85643/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db0fcba2-580a-5416-a4f3-af3297439442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85643/selection/02bd85d8ef0eab243b5263b64b9ff5a329de46d7086d62c76e90e0b6d5401f96" :answer-field/choices ["q-85643/selection/02bd85d8ef0eab243b5263b64b9ff5a329de46d7086d62c76e90e0b6d5401f96" "q-85643/selection/a3d13a5807221d895018d7b06558d926d62bfb001b459077c27b527e0d873fba" "q-85643/selection/2ddda6672cd9117c496b40039bb24e9551b86514a0ced6b2d869664914795cff" "q-85643/selection/fbc9f6433e70c687e4cd524a01759124f3a0b394750ef110b890774618ad4f45" "q-85643/selection/250d160b15e9359628e412b91e5c1fd679c52d57a82017145d130d6c7fa4646e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85643" :question/id #uuid "0902cd66-9d18-50eb-a894-3b1edfc4b17b" :question/math-academy-id "q-85643" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/3be6fa94deb7fc38d870e5a31cc81c3cfd6b9ab84c21340e7e88f7246b1058bc.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{5}{7},$ what is the value of $sec⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/17e6320115f2cf8b5ffad6abc099169774536af20d2559b453aaa97c1286d96d.png)\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{5}{7}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{7}.$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{5}{7})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{25}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{24}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{24}}{7} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7})}=-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{6}}=-\\frac{7\\sqrt{6}}{12}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85643/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a09362-632a-56c4-b246-903e18fc77ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85641/selection/138399153e3da3b1ac41abb4f59b1ec141ad5860bc977350624d8342147d2ded" :answer/id #uuid "44c9bab2-94b2-52c1-bc5e-6235db012a7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85641/selection/83d3d87b235ae4b8cabc62ba44d2672c0c8edfba4dc99528ce8a309c17250a29" :answer/id #uuid "48a01b4d-e2c7-5f6c-b388-0e1a527bebb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85641/selection/f500f1a71c0d79daa4ed62981f336fec820a112b0da421f6028092d7af4e3312" :answer/id #uuid "a4f81c0b-2967-5a6e-a74a-2763b2e55dfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85641/selection/956deceb93b791a0ccee98cb58ee444c3a2cd860a34d9692502b811dafee9186" :answer/id #uuid "d4c7f755-77f7-57b2-b14c-c305aa4561e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85641/selection/4103ea40286243cc3a782516b29370383d8ade56d1f2d9714537501bb561b226" :answer/id #uuid "492eab21-3fb0-54c0-92c6-a731710f234b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85641/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bee8e07c-bea9-57ef-8ea7-55ee192590f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85641/selection/4103ea40286243cc3a782516b29370383d8ade56d1f2d9714537501bb561b226" :answer-field/choices ["q-85641/selection/138399153e3da3b1ac41abb4f59b1ec141ad5860bc977350624d8342147d2ded" "q-85641/selection/83d3d87b235ae4b8cabc62ba44d2672c0c8edfba4dc99528ce8a309c17250a29" "q-85641/selection/f500f1a71c0d79daa4ed62981f336fec820a112b0da421f6028092d7af4e3312" "q-85641/selection/956deceb93b791a0ccee98cb58ee444c3a2cd860a34d9692502b811dafee9186" "q-85641/selection/4103ea40286243cc3a782516b29370383d8ade56d1f2d9714537501bb561b226"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85641" :question/id #uuid "7e671aac-3a60-5948-a969-9b2f942ef09c" :question/math-academy-id "q-85641" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/9d879cc44b4c3949f38584482261cba8c97a58457ffeb611bfd313b7b3194b0a.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},$ what is the value of $sec⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/b79868db47bbe4ef308975cea659dc7b964ae7fcf894ee92bbb9ee8070dcaac1.png)\n\nWe're given that $y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{5}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the positive answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is positive in the fourth quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{2}{3})}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85641/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a09362-632a-56c4-b246-903e18fc77ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85641"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125004/selection/75623852529657b9e2e8f5776f67bdb6ef780f77779181105fe9da3ab47ff136" :answer/id #uuid "706dc955-dc51-5468-b03b-22112ebb4568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125004/selection/32561e62dcb45e535d108e54ffce93fba868da802b96ffbcb59b1069068602c6" :answer/id #uuid "d91ba099-7743-5942-9cf0-694b5a2d9cec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125004/selection/0640f06a6b8668e675902a5654153f1be90aa161eebbd90df124f83febaa7af1" :answer/id #uuid "c7c24e3d-6803-5199-97e1-bd13410dc9e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =8\\sqrt{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125004/selection/b27da784cda5135f945782dfb035d7b94b4cf76140f646ffb319ddb492661da2" :answer/id #uuid "de5028d1-048e-518e-b4dd-482c0872a56b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{4\\sqrt{15}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125004/selection/eeed1efb8d42d3f794a53d7b51b9657b0803d75c01e0ae53d84d2ebbc8bed908" :answer/id #uuid "eba51077-bb3f-52cf-ade7-6ecc08816110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-8\\sqrt{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125004/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c5cf0b1-5600-5e1e-a6d7-f7cac1c521dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125004/selection/75623852529657b9e2e8f5776f67bdb6ef780f77779181105fe9da3ab47ff136" :answer-field/choices ["q-125004/selection/75623852529657b9e2e8f5776f67bdb6ef780f77779181105fe9da3ab47ff136" "q-125004/selection/32561e62dcb45e535d108e54ffce93fba868da802b96ffbcb59b1069068602c6" "q-125004/selection/0640f06a6b8668e675902a5654153f1be90aa161eebbd90df124f83febaa7af1" "q-125004/selection/b27da784cda5135f945782dfb035d7b94b4cf76140f646ffb319ddb492661da2" "q-125004/selection/eeed1efb8d42d3f794a53d7b51b9657b0803d75c01e0ae53d84d2ebbc8bed908"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125004" :question/id #uuid "c006e542-29a2-5102-8308-98f4920ebd17" :question/math-academy-id "q-125004" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\theta <\\pi $ then what is the value of $sec⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch our angle $\\theta $ in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/5c98414bbe0e1e373864e9ec1d6b8667bb0032c8824f20bed1e6f9b9079c4d02.png)\n\nWe're given that $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}.$ We can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{49}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8})}=-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{15}}=-\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{15}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-125004/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a09362-632a-56c4-b246-903e18fc77ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125004"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85649/selection/4f647c4bb2c448b4cbaa120a8825192c1d364c937b02f862c8766bdfff008711" :answer/id #uuid "8d71834d-59e3-57b4-86ec-3e6080269d03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85649/selection/326ec81f8d52a2dc9bbe4253461f976320471befa4a3a8b77599551649301c90" :answer/id #uuid "46a30282-7d3f-56ba-9a99-e669ed7a5e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85649/selection/4f0069b983a861a6de1e0ccf11d1869d40cf8f9546bfffaafb4fe5afbe733579" :answer/id #uuid "57b9d878-5132-5c86-925b-32a92dfdd9ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85649/selection/f27c09041070ac01c06af3d856d67880d064eac40dceaa7ffd32729e5656bd61" :answer/id #uuid "40b81b0f-e8ee-5524-be62-4247258088fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{8\\sqrt{7}}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85649/selection/0b736d6745c45096df85ca5dd464bae90b9b893dc043b5a2b3cd57ba518a9abe" :answer/id #uuid "0ac158b4-7c0a-58e8-949d-7db5d27652d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85649/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c44c19a6-8c24-5e98-a45e-74d07f9eaefc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85649/selection/f27c09041070ac01c06af3d856d67880d064eac40dceaa7ffd32729e5656bd61" :answer-field/choices ["q-85649/selection/4f647c4bb2c448b4cbaa120a8825192c1d364c937b02f862c8766bdfff008711" "q-85649/selection/326ec81f8d52a2dc9bbe4253461f976320471befa4a3a8b77599551649301c90" "q-85649/selection/4f0069b983a861a6de1e0ccf11d1869d40cf8f9546bfffaafb4fe5afbe733579" "q-85649/selection/f27c09041070ac01c06af3d856d67880d064eac40dceaa7ffd32729e5656bd61" "q-85649/selection/0b736d6745c45096df85ca5dd464bae90b9b893dc043b5a2b3cd57ba518a9abe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85649" :question/id #uuid "a15b0347-c7e8-56db-a50a-1d56900c2170" :question/math-academy-id "q-85649" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/cd41c969aee2e7c04c9034106978d8522d6a715733098bfde87abbdb861da7a8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{1}{8},$ what is the value of $sec⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/4942cec8983dd2bddddd0ba2f8f9332b1b82f3999a44adb138b905457d39c633.png)\n\nWe're given that $y=\\frac{1}{8}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{8}.$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{8}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{63}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{63}}{8} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{8}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{8})}=-\\frac{8}{3\\sqrt{7}}=-\\frac{8\\sqrt{7}}{21}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85649/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a09362-632a-56c4-b246-903e18fc77ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85649"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85642/selection/0f5b35f862d5cc9b9104503b83387cfbc5ba350ace72debeb2ed16866832b009" :answer/id #uuid "f362d121-8787-5369-933a-4c74b57361ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "csc⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85642/selection/09304a2365e07d363e27997bba27380e628fddb538ce3378fad477a9dad6aa62" :answer/id #uuid "60fe65a8-b139-5de1-92a2-f1c282bb17ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "csc⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85642/selection/e42c5624941d5cd89d0f31a980426d68c3b771eb4512cdcd5a31f910088f3585" :answer/id #uuid "c612bfa0-bace-5469-8960-152a2e1372aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "csc⁡\\theta =-\\frac{4\\sqrt{15}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85642/selection/7a6e12ac06a4a990f6c250377649972032514231996feb50b7889b780e12585d" :answer/id #uuid "8295e07f-60f7-5394-8cd2-aa6f2330f534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "csc⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{15}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85642/selection/58f4c15d7c879ad9346c357f41efea9d733d7c5e3828c4c70ecc9c1cbe11bfd0" :answer/id #uuid "49e5c347-96bc-53cf-8dd8-acdaf1551de4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "csc⁡\\theta =\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85642/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4aba410c-61c1-5e3d-b11a-7b607a678449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85642/selection/e42c5624941d5cd89d0f31a980426d68c3b771eb4512cdcd5a31f910088f3585" :answer-field/choices ["q-85642/selection/0f5b35f862d5cc9b9104503b83387cfbc5ba350ace72debeb2ed16866832b009" "q-85642/selection/09304a2365e07d363e27997bba27380e628fddb538ce3378fad477a9dad6aa62" "q-85642/selection/e42c5624941d5cd89d0f31a980426d68c3b771eb4512cdcd5a31f910088f3585" "q-85642/selection/7a6e12ac06a4a990f6c250377649972032514231996feb50b7889b780e12585d" "q-85642/selection/58f4c15d7c879ad9346c357f41efea9d733d7c5e3828c4c70ecc9c1cbe11bfd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85642" :question/id #uuid "bd526035-dea8-5fa0-8a08-1ec8fea39cc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-85642" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/75b3a8b6aa11ac54edd5e3f0d694514cf7e63eefd05313ab854ddd917aa32ad5.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{1}{4},$ use the Pythagorean identity to find $csc⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932638/assets/73972bbedd114db6635eaec98dd0989f7d6e877aa276b381973b753204e2b8e8.png)\n\nWe're given that $x=\\frac{1}{4}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $sin⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the negative answer since $sin⁡\\theta $ is negative in the fourth quadrant. So $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $csc⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{sin⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ncsc⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4})}=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{15}}=-\\frac{4\\sqrt{15}}{15}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85642/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a09362-632a-56c4-b246-903e18fc77ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
